No big spoiler really.  You entered a graveyard.  It's just a room
like a zoo, except that it is full of undead things.  The ghosts 
weren't from a bones level, so the names weren't ones you used
before.  Nethack has a list of names to use for ghosts (I think it
also gets them from the highscore list sometimes).

The main thing of value in a graveyard are the wraiths -- their corpses
let you gain a level.  So it would be good idea to at least kill the 
wraiths and eat them.

With zoos & graveyards, the big things that help you are either a 
ring of conflict or stealth (ring, elven cloak, intrinsic, ...).
If you have stealth you can enter the room, and the monsters don't
wake up, so you can attack them all one on one.

Aside from stealth and conflict, the standard things will help you:
better armor, better weapons, speed,...  Protection from level drain
is also a nice thing to have (although monsters seldom seem to level 
drain me in 3.0j -- I think they used to a lot more in older versions).
 
If you stumble into a graveyard and really can't handle it, I'd say
try engraving "Elbereth" in the doorway and run away to the next
level (undead things are all affected by it, I think).  Failing that,
just run.

